doupdate's line-breakout typeahead check ran twice back to back: once before
the line loop and again at line 0, because the counter started at
CHECK_INTERVAL. Nothing is written between the two, so the second answer is
the first one again; the counter now starts at 0 (next check after 5 changed
lines, as between the later checks). Each check is a select() -> ixemul
WaitForChar(fh, 0) round trip to the console handler (~27 ms on the A1200
rig under vtcon), so a 1-line keystroke paid two. Output bytes unchanged.
Independent of the other ncurses patches; apply in any order, with -p1 inside ncurses/.
--- a/tty/tty_update.c	2026-10-19 12:59:40
+++ b/tty/tty_update.c	2026-10-19 17:29:45
@@ -1016,7 +1016,13 @@
 	CurScreen(SP_PARM)->_clear = FALSE;	/* reset flag */
 	NewScreen(SP_PARM)->_clear = FALSE;	/* reset flag */
     } else {
-	int changedlines = CHECK_INTERVAL;
+	/*
+	 * The check below is the first of the line-breakout checks, so the
+	 * counter starts at zero: starting it at CHECK_INTERVAL repeated the
+	 * check at line 0 with nothing written in between.  A check is a
+	 * console round trip (select/WaitForChar), not free.
+	 */
+	int changedlines = 0;
 
 	if (check_pending(NCURSES_SP_ARG))
 	    goto cleanup;
